{%- comment -%} ===================== App connection ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-app-connection" data-group="Help" data-title="App can't find or keep EXO" data-time="4 min"
  data-keywords="app bluetooth pair find exo offline disconnect phone connect no device connected">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>App can't find or keep EXO</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix pairing and Bluetooth problems between your phone and EXO.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">iPhone</span><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Android</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>
  <p>Start here: is your app up to date? See <a href="#p-start-updates">Keep EXO up to date</a>.</p>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-app-connection--cant-find-exo">
    <h2>The app can't find my EXO</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The EXO has no power, Bluetooth is off, or the phone didn't get to pick ZeroStick EXO.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check the EXO logo is lit. If not, make sure the CONSOLE cable goes to a console or PC that's switched on.</li>
        <li>Turn on Bluetooth on your phone.</li>
        <li>Allow the ZeroStick app to use Bluetooth in your phone's settings.</li>
        <li>Move your phone close to the EXO.</li>
        <li>In the app, tap <b>Connect</b> and choose <b>ZeroStick EXO</b> in the list.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gs-not-found.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="742" loading="lazy"
        alt="Connect to your ZeroStick: your EXO was not found nearby. 1: Try again. 2: Use a different EXO.">
      <figcaption>Figure APP-CONN.1 — Your EXO was not found nearby</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Try again</b></td><td>Check the EXO is plugged in and powered, then tap here.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Use a different EXO</b></td><td>Only to connect to another EXO.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The EXO card on HOME says <b>Connected</b>.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Try <a href="#p-help-reset--forget-and-repair">forget and pair again</a>, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-app-connection--app-says-offline">
    <h2>The app says Offline</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The phone lost its Bluetooth link: it's too far away, Bluetooth is off, or the EXO lost power.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check the EXO logo is lit.</li>
        <li>Check Bluetooth is on.</li>
        <li>Bring your phone closer to the EXO.</li>
        <li>Close the app fully and open it again.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gs-home-offline.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME with the EXO off. 1: the ZeroStick EXO card says Offline.">
      <figcaption>Figure APP-CONN.2 — HOME, EXO offline</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Offline</b></td><td>Check the EXO's cable and power.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME's EXO card changes from <b>Offline</b> to <b>Connected</b>.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-help-app-connection--cant-find-exo">The app can't find my EXO</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-app-connection--changes-didnt-save">
    <h2>My changes didn't save</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The EXO was offline when you made the change. Changes wait in the app and sync when it reconnects.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Reconnect the app (HOME should say <b>Connected</b>).</li>
        <li>Wait a few seconds for the sync.</li>
        <li>Open the setting again to check it.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gs-home.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME with the EXO connected. 1: Settings. 2: the three-dot More button. 3: the devices plugged into the EXO. 4: the ZeroStick EXO card, Connected. 5: the Active weapon card.">
      <figcaption>Figure APP-CONN.3 — HOME: card 4 should say Connected</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Settings</b></td><td>Everything for the config that's playing: aim, mappings, Scripts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>⋮ (More)</b></td><td>Your configs, new config and Global Settings.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Device pictures</b></td><td>What's plugged into the EXO. Tap one to see it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>ZeroStick EXO card</b></td><td><b>Connected</b>, the console mode and what you play with.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">5</span></td><td><b>Active weapon</b></td><td>The gun the EXO sees in your game, and its AI Scripts.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The setting shows your new value, and the game feels the change.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with a screenshot of the setting.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-app-connection--exo-restarted">
    <h2>HOME says "Your EXO restarted unexpectedly"</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The EXO restarted by itself, often from a power dip.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Tap the yellow <b>!</b> chip, if there is one, and read the warning.</li>
        <li>If it's a power warning, add power on <a href="#p-platforms-power--aux">AUX/POWER</a>.</li>
        <li>Tap <b>Send report</b> (1) to copy a report, and email it to us.</li>
        <li>Tap <b>Dismiss</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-dv-health.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="416" loading="lazy"
        alt="Part of HOME: Your EXO restarted unexpectedly. 1: Send report. 2: Dismiss.">
      <figcaption>Figure APP-CONN.4 — HOME after an unexpected restart</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Send report</b></td><td>Copies a plain-text report. Nothing is uploaded.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Dismiss</b></td><td>Hides the message.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The message doesn't come back while you play.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Send the report to <a href="#support-email"><span data-m2-email>caleb@zerostickgaming.com</span></a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== PS5 ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-ps5" data-group="Help" data-title="PS5 problems" data-time="4 min"
  data-keywords="ps5 problems not working controller does nothing auth dongle wrong mode headset no sound no picture hdmi">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>PS5 problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix the most common problems on PS5, quickest fix first.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PS5</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-ps5--controller-not-working">
    <h2>Nothing happens on my PS5</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The config is set to another console, the auth dongle isn't in AUTH, or a cable is loose.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check HOME's EXO card says <b>PS5 Mode</b>. If not, see <a href="#p-help-ps5--wrong-mode">the wrong mode</a>.</li>
        <li>Check the PS5 auth dongle is in <b>AUTH</b>.</li>
        <li>Check the CONSOLE cable is firmly in the EXO and the PS5.</li>
        <li>Check your controls are in the front ports and show at the top of HOME.</li>
        <li>Unplug the CONSOLE cable, wait 5 seconds, and plug it back in.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-back.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="339" loading="lazy"
        alt="The back of the EXO, left to right: CONSOLE, AUX/POWER, AUTH, HDMI IN and HDMI OUT.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PS5.1 — The back of the EXO, every port named</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your controls move around the PS5 menus.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> and send a screenshot of HOME.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-ps5--wrong-mode">
    <h2>HOME shows the wrong mode</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The playing config's Connection Method is set to another console.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Device</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the console row under <b>Connection Method</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the arrows until it shows <b>PlayStation 5</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cc-ps5-chosen.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="356" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Connection Method card reading PlayStation 5. 1: the console row.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PS5.2 — Connection Method set to PlayStation 5</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>PlayStation 5</b></td><td>Tap to change it.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME shows <b>PS5 Mode</b>, <b>Xbox Mode</b> or <b>PC Mode</b> to match your console.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Check you changed the config that's <b>PLAYING</b> in <a href="#p-app-configs--switch">Your configs</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-ps5--dongle-not-seen">
    <h2>The PS5 doesn't accept the EXO</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The PS5 auth dongle is missing, loose or in the wrong port.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Unplug the dongle.</li>
        <li>Plug it firmly into <b>AUTH</b> (the USB-A port on the back), not a front port.</li>
        <li>Unplug the CONSOLE cable, wait 5 seconds, and plug it back in.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-auth.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the AUTH USB-A port marked.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PS5.3 — AUTH, on the back: the dongle goes here, not in a front port</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your controls move around the PS5 menus.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a>. Tell us you're on PS5 and what HOME shows.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-ps5--headset-no-sound">
    <h2>No sound in my headset</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The headset is in the wrong place, or the PS5's volume or mute is set low.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Plug your headset into your DualSense, not into the EXO.</li>
        <li>Check the DualSense is plugged into a front port with a USB cable.</li>
        <li>Check the PS5's volume and mute in its sound controls.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-front.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="265" loading="lazy"
        alt="The front of the EXO. One USB-C port on the left and three USB-A ports, for controllers, a mouse and a keyboard.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PS5.4 — Your DualSense goes into a front port; your headset goes into the DualSense</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>You hear the game, and friends hear you in party chat.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Headset support is in final validation on first units. Please <a href="#p-help-get-support">tell us</a> your headset model.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-ps5--no-picture">
    <h2>No picture on my TV</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The HDMI cables are swapped or loose.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check the cable from your console goes into <b>HDMI IN</b>.</li>
        <li>Check the cable to your TV goes into <b>HDMI OUT</b>.</li>
        <li>Push both cables in firmly at each end.</li>
        <li>Check your TV is on the right input.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-hdmi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="599" loading="lazy"
        alt="The two HDMI ports on the back of the EXO. HDMI IN takes the cable from your console. HDMI OUT goes to your TV.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PS5.5 — HDMI IN from the console, HDMI OUT to the TV</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your console's picture shows on the TV.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Plug the console straight into the TV to test the cable, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Xbox ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-xbox" data-group="Help" data-title="Xbox problems" data-time="3 min"
  data-keywords="xbox problems not working controller auth wrong mode update">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Xbox problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix the most common problems on Xbox, quickest fix first.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Xbox</span><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-xbox--controller-not-working">
    <h2>Nothing happens on my Xbox</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The config is set to another console, the controller in AUTH isn't connected, or a cable is loose.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check HOME's EXO card says <b>Xbox Mode</b>. If not, see <a href="#p-help-xbox--wrong-mode">the wrong mode</a>.</li>
        <li>Check your genuine Xbox controller is in <b>AUTH</b> with its USB cable.</li>
        <li>Check the CONSOLE cable is firmly in the EXO and the Xbox.</li>
        <li>Unplug the CONSOLE cable, wait 5 seconds, and plug it back in.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-back.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="339" loading="lazy"
        alt="The back of the EXO, left to right: CONSOLE, AUX/POWER, AUTH, HDMI IN and HDMI OUT.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-XBOX.1 — The back of the EXO, every port named</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your controls move around the Xbox menus.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> and tell us your Xbox controller model.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-xbox--wrong-mode">
    <h2>HOME shows the wrong mode</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The playing config's Connection Method is set to another console.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Device</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the <b>Connection Method</b> row.</li>
        <li>Tap <b>Xbox</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cc-card.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="891" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Connection Method card on the Device page. 1: the console row (here PC). 2: What you play with. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-XBOX.2 — Settings › Device › Connection Method</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Console row</b></td><td>Tap to pick your console.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>What you play with</b></td><td><b>Auto</b>, <b>Mouse + Keyboard</b>, <b>Controller</b> or <b>Joystick + Mouse</b>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>The app's own explanation.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME shows <b>Xbox Mode</b>.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Check you changed the config that's <b>PLAYING</b> in <a href="#p-app-configs--switch">Your configs</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-xbox--controller-update">
    <h2>My controller in AUTH wants an update</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The Xbox offers controller updates now and then.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Don't accept the update while the controller is in AUTH.</li>
        <li>Unplug the controller from the EXO.</li>
        <li>Update it straight on the Xbox, then plug it back into AUTH.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-auth.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the AUTH USB-A port marked.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-XBOX.3 — AUTH, the USB-A port on the back</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The controller is up to date and your controls work again.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-xbox--no-picture">
    <h2>No picture on my TV</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The HDMI cables are swapped or loose.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check the cable from your Xbox goes into <b>HDMI IN</b>.</li>
        <li>Check the cable to your TV goes into <b>HDMI OUT</b>.</li>
        <li>Push both cables in firmly, and check the TV input.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-hdmi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="599" loading="lazy"
        alt="The two HDMI ports on the back of the EXO. HDMI IN takes the cable from your console. HDMI OUT goes to your TV.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-XBOX.4 — HDMI IN from the console, HDMI OUT to the TV</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your Xbox's picture shows on the TV.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Plug the Xbox straight into the TV to test the cable, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== PC ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-pc" data-group="Help" data-title="PC problems" data-time="2 min"
  data-keywords="pc windows problems controller not detected not seen wrong mode steam">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>PC problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix the most common problems on a Windows PC.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">PC</span><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-pc--not-seen">
    <h2>Windows doesn't see a controller</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The play cable is in AUX/POWER instead of CONSOLE, or the config is set to another console.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Move the PC cable into <b>CONSOLE</b> on the EXO.</li>
        <li>Check HOME says <b>PC Mode</b>. If not, see <a href="#p-help-pc--wrong-mode">the wrong mode</a>.</li>
        <li>Try another USB port on the PC.</li>
        <li>Check your game is set to use a controller.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-console.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the CONSOLE USB-C port marked. It goes to your console or PC.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PC.1 — The PC cable goes into CONSOLE</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your game or Steam reacts to the EXO like a controller.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with your Windows version.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-pc--wrong-mode">
    <h2>HOME shows the wrong mode</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The playing config's Connection Method is set to a console.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>On HOME, tap <b>Settings</b>, then <b>Device</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the console row under <b>Connection Method</b>.</li>
        <li>Tap the arrows (1) until it shows <b>PC</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cc-pick-pc.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="635" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Console Connection panel on PC. 1: the arrow.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-PC.2 — Console Connection on PC</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Arrows</b></td><td>Go through the consoles.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME shows <b>PC Mode</b>.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Check you changed the config that's <b>PLAYING</b> in <a href="#p-app-configs--switch">Your configs</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Aim feels wrong ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong" data-group="Help" data-title="Aim feels off" data-time="5 min"
  data-keywords="aim feels wrong off sens sensitivity too fast too slow floaty laggy jitter small moves ignored ads different vertical">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Aim feels off</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Match the feeling to a fix. Change one setting at a time.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">5 min</span></div>
  </header>
  <p>Start here: are your <a href="#p-aim-game-settings">in-game settings</a> set the way the app asks? Most aim problems start there.</p>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--too-fast-or-slow">
    <h2>My aim is too fast or too slow</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The game's sensitivity doesn't match the app's list, the mouse DPI in the app is wrong, or Speed needs a change.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Set your in-game settings exactly as the app lists them.</li>
        <li>Check <b>Mouse DPI</b> on the Device page matches your mouse. Tap <b>Measure my DPI</b> if unsure.</li>
        <li>In <b>Aim</b>, raise <b>Speed</b> if turning feels slow, or lower it if you overshoot.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-speed.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1128" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim, Speed 64.2 (3), about 12.2 cm per 360.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.1 — Settings › Aim › Hip aim: Speed is 3</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Speed</b></td><td>Higher turns faster for the same hand movement.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>A comfortable mouse swipe turns you the amount you expect.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--aim-feels-floaty">
    <h2>My aim feels floaty</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Too much smoothing, or Sync to game doesn't match the game's frame rate.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>In <b>Aim</b>, set <b>Smoothing</b> to <b>Disabled</b> or <b>Light</b>.</li>
        <li>In <b>Advanced</b> › <b>Translation</b>, set <b>Sync to game</b> to the frame rate you play at.</li>
        <li>In Aim's Advanced settings, check <b>Feel</b> is <b>Snappy</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-smoothing.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1128" loading="lazy"
        alt="Hip aim, Smoothing Disabled. 1: the arrow to change it.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.2 — Settings › Aim: Smoothing</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Smoothing</b></td><td>Step through the presets.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-tr-sync.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Translation, Advanced, Sync to game with 60, 120, Custom and Off. 2: Sync to game.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.3 — Translation › Advanced › Sync to game</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Sync to game</b></td><td>Pick your game's frame rate.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The view stops the moment your hand stops.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-reference-settings--aim">every aim setting</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--small-moves-ignored">
    <h2>Small mouse moves are ignored</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd><b>Ignore tiny movement</b> is set too high, or the game's deadzone setting doesn't match.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>In Aim's Advanced settings, set <b>Ignore tiny movement</b> to 0.</li>
        <li>Set the game's deadzone to the value on the app's list.</li>
        <li>Try raising <b>Fine aim</b> a little.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-feel.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The bottom of Advanced. 1: Ignore tiny movement. 3: Feel.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.4 — Aim › Advanced: Ignore tiny movement is 1</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Ignore tiny movement</b></td><td>Set it to 0.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Feel</b></td><td>Snappy, Balanced or Smooth.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Tiny hand movements nudge your crosshair.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-aim-mouse">Mouse aim settings</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--ads-feels-different">
    <h2>Aiming down sights feels different from hip fire</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>ADS has its own Speed, or the switch from hip to ADS happens too early.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>In <b>Aim</b>, tap <b>ADS aim</b>.</li>
        <li>Set ADS <b>Speed</b> to <b>Same as hip</b>, or adjust it.</li>
        <li>Open <b>Activation</b> and set <b>Activate</b> to match how long your game takes to zoom in.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ma-activation.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="ADS aim tab, Activation open. 1: ADS aim. 2: Activation. 3: Activate, 0 ms. 4: Deactivate, 0 ms. 5: Smooth ADS Transition help.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.5 — Settings › Aim › ADS aim › Activation</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>ADS aim</b></td><td>The settings used while you aim.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Activation</b></td><td>Tap to open the card.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Activate</b></td><td>How long the game takes to zoom in.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Deactivate</b></td><td>How long it takes to zoom out.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">5</span></td><td><b>Smooth ADS Transition</b></td><td>Tap ? to see what it does.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Aiming in feels as steady as hip fire.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-aim-hip-and-ads">Hip fire and ADS</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--vertical-different">
    <h2>Up and down feels different from left and right</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd><b>Y Scale</b> isn't 100, or the game's vertical sensitivity is changed.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Set the game's vertical sensitivity as the app lists it.</li>
        <li>In Aim's Advanced settings, set <b>Y Scale</b> to 100.</li>
        <li>Then adjust Y Scale in small steps if you still want a change.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-cf-sheet.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Your game settings sheet, marked REQUIRED, with the rows to set in the game. 1: your stick sensitivity boxes. 2: Your in-game FOV. 3: the help button.">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.6 — Your game settings: the vertical sensitivity box is part of 1</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Your stick sensitivity</b></td><td>Type the sensitivity you set in the game (4.00 recommended).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Your in-game FOV</b></td><td>Type the field of view you play at.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>?</b></td><td>Why these must match the game.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Looking up and down feels as fast as turning.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-reference-settings--aim">every aim setting</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-aim-feels-wrong--aim-jitters">
    <h2>My aim jitters</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The mouse sensor is dirty, the surface is shiny, or the wireless signal is weak.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Clean the mouse sensor and use a mouse pad.</li>
        <li>Move a wireless dongle closer to the mouse, or use a hub on your desk.</li>
        <li>Run <b>Check rate (Hz)</b> on the Device page.</li>
        <li>Add a little <b>Smoothing</b> if it still jitters.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sm-dpi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="831" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Mouse DPI card. 1: the DPI presets, 3,200 recommended. 2: Measure my DPI. 3: Check rate (Hz).">
      <figcaption>Figure FEEL-WRON.7 — Settings › Device › Mouse DPI: Check rate (Hz) is 3</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>DPI presets</b></td><td>Tap your mouse's DPI, or type it in the box.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Measure my DPI</b></td><td>The app finds it with a short guided move.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Check rate (Hz)</b></td><td>Tests your mouse's polling rate.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>A still mouse gives a still crosshair.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-help-mouse-and-keyboard--mouse-skips">Mouse skips or feels laggy</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Mouse and keyboard ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-mouse-and-keyboard" data-group="Help" data-title="Mouse or keyboard problems" data-time="4 min"
  data-keywords="mouse keyboard not detected wireless dongle polling rate lag skip wrong keys chat typing pass-through">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Mouse or keyboard problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix devices that don't show up, skip, or do the wrong thing.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="x2-badge x2-badge--plain">Mouse &amp; keyboard</span><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-mouse-and-keyboard--not-detected">
    <h2>My mouse or keyboard isn't detected</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>A loose plug, a hub that can't keep up, or not enough power.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Unplug the device and plug it into another front port.</li>
        <li>If you use a hub, plug the device straight into the EXO to test.</li>
        <li>Add power on <a href="#p-platforms-power--aux">AUX/POWER</a>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-front.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="265" loading="lazy"
        alt="The front of the EXO. One USB-C port on the left and three USB-A ports, for controllers, a mouse and a keyboard.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-KEYB.1 — The front of the EXO: one USB-C port and three USB-A ports</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The device's picture shows at the top of HOME.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with the device's make and model.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-mouse-and-keyboard--mouse-skips">
    <h2>My mouse skips or feels laggy</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>A weak wireless signal, or the mouse's polling rate is set low.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Move the wireless dongle closer to your mouse.</li>
        <li>On the Device page, tap <b>Check rate (Hz)</b> and follow the steps.</li>
        <li>Set your mouse to 1000 Hz in its own software, if it can.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sm-dpi.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="831" loading="lazy"
        alt="The Mouse DPI card. 1: the DPI presets, 3,200 recommended. 2: Measure my DPI. 3: Check rate (Hz).">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-KEYB.2 — Mouse DPI card: Check rate (Hz) is 3</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>DPI presets</b></td><td>Tap your mouse's DPI, or type it in the box.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Measure my DPI</b></td><td>The app finds it with a short guided move.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Check rate (Hz)</b></td><td>Tests your mouse's polling rate.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The rate check shows about 1000 Hz and the crosshair moves smoothly.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Try the mouse with a cable, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-mouse-and-keyboard--wrong-keys">
    <h2>Keys or clicks do the wrong thing</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>A mapping changed, or you're on a different config than you think.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check HOME shows the config you meant.</li>
        <li>Open <b>Settings</b> › <b>Mappings</b> and check the key.</li>
        <li>Change it back. See <a href="#p-controls-mappings">Remap buttons and keys</a>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-keys.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Mappings, Mouse and Keyboard. 1: Showing Mouse and Keyboard, Switch. 2: Bigger keys. 3: the W row, Left Stick Up.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-KEYB.3 — Settings › Mappings › Mouse &amp; Keyboard</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Switch</b></td><td>Go to the controller view.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Bigger keys</b></td><td>A bigger keyboard picture. Tap a key to change it.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>A binding row</b></td><td>Here W sends Left Stick Up.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The key does what you expect in the game.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Check no Script uses that key: see <a href="#p-help-scripts--script-wont-stop">A Script won't stop</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-mouse-and-keyboard--passthrough-not-switching">
    <h2>I can't type in chat (Pass-through doesn't switch)</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd><b>Shortcut buttons</b> is off, or the shortcut was changed.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Open <b>⋮</b> › <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b>.</li>
        <li>Check <b>Shortcut buttons</b> is on.</li>
        <li>Check the shortcut on the Pass-through card. The default is <span class="m2-key">1</span> + <span class="m2-key">5</span>.</li>
        <li>Press both keys at the same time.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-passthrough-card-m2.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="1091" loading="lazy"
        alt="Global Settings, General tab, Pass-through card with the 1 plus 5 shortcut. 1: Edit shortcut. 2: Turn on. 3: Shortcut buttons switch, on.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-KEYB.4 — Global Settings › General › Pass-through</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Edit shortcut</b></td><td>Change the keys.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Turn on</b></td><td>Start it from the app.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Shortcut buttons</b></td><td>Must be on for the keys to work.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME shows <b>Passthrough mode active</b> and you can type.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Tap <b>Turn on</b> on the Pass-through card instead, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Gun detection ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-gun-detection" data-group="Help" data-title="Gun detection problems" data-time="4 min"
  data-keywords="gun detection ai scripts no gun detected wrong gun weapon active weapon hdmi frame hud">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Gun detection problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix automatic gun detection when it sees nothing, or the wrong gun.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">4 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-gun-detection--no-gun-detected">
    <h2>No gun is detected</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>HDMI isn't looped through the EXO, the game doesn't have gun detection, or the gun reader frame is in the wrong place.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check the console's HDMI goes into <b>HDMI IN</b> and <b>HDMI OUT</b> goes to the TV.</li>
        <li>Check your game has gun detection in the <a href="#games">supported games list</a>.</li>
        <li>Check you're in a match with a gun out. Menus pause detection.</li>
        <li>Open <b>AI Scripts</b> and set the <b>Gun reader frame</b> around your HUD's gun name.</li>
        <li>Check Tournament Mode is off.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ai-capture.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Gun reader frame, Step 1. 1: Start frame capture.">
      <figcaption>Figure GUN-DETE.1 — AI Scripts › Gun reader frame</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Start frame capture</b></td><td>Takes a picture of your screen to set the frame.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>HOME's <b>Active weapon</b> card shows the gun in your hands.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-auto-gun-detection">Automatic gun detection</a>, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-gun-detection--wrong-gun">
    <h2>The wrong gun is detected</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The gun reader frame catches other text, or your HUD layout changed.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Open <b>AI Scripts</b> › <b>Gun reader frame</b>.</li>
        <li>Make the frame fit just around the gun name.</li>
        <li>Check your in-game HUD settings match the app's list.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ai-match.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Gun reader frame, Match the box: the example shows the box tight around the gun name.">
      <figcaption>Figure GUN-DETE.2 — Match the box: fit it around the gun name only</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The Active weapon card changes to the right gun when you swap.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with the game and gun names.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-gun-detection--paused-in-menus">
    <h2>Detection stops in menus</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>That's normal. With no gun on screen, gun Scripts pause so they can't fire by mistake.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps"><li>Go back into a match and take out a gun.</li></ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-ai-home-menu.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="389" loading="lazy"
        alt="HOME, Active weapon card: Menu or paused, waiting for your weapon. 1: the card.">
      <figcaption>Figure GUN-DETE.3 — HOME in a menu</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Active weapon</b></td><td>AI Scripts pause until a weapon is back on screen.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The Active weapon card shows your gun again.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-help-gun-detection--no-gun-detected">No gun is detected</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Scripts ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-scripts" data-group="Help" data-title="Script problems" data-time="3 min"
  data-keywords="script wont fire not working wont stop stuck tournament mode">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Script problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix Scripts that won't start, or won't stop.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-scripts--script-wont-fire">
    <h2>A Script won't fire</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Tournament Mode is on, the Script's switch is off, or it only runs while aiming down sights.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Check Tournament Mode is off: <b>⋮</b> › <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b>.</li>
        <li>Check the Script's switch is on.</li>
        <li>Check what starts it (its <b>WHEN</b> part) in the Advanced Script Maker.</li>
        <li>For a per-gun Script, check the Active weapon card shows that gun.</li>
        <li>Tap the EXO card on HOME and check <b>Adapter is sending inputs</b> says <b>On</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-mp-list.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Mappings, the Scripts list for this config. 1: Scripts, 3 on this config. 2: a Script's on and off switch. 3: Add a button.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-SCRI.1 — Settings › Mappings › Scripts</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Scripts</b></td><td>Shows or hides the Scripts on this config.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">2</span></td><td><b>Switch</b></td><td>Turns one Script on or off.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">3</span></td><td><b>Add a button</b></td><td>Gives another button its own mapping or Script.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The Script does its job when you press its trigger.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>See <a href="#p-scripts-library">Scripts</a>, or <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a> with the Script's share code.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-scripts--script-wont-stop">
    <h2>A Script won't stop</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>It's set to toggle, so it runs until you press its trigger again.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Press the Script's trigger again.</li>
        <li>To stop everything at once, turn on <b>Tournament Mode</b>.</li>
        <li>Turn the Script's switch off, then check its <b>WHEN</b> part.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gl-tournament.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="432" loading="lazy"
        alt="Global Settings, General tab. 1: the Tournament Mode switch, on.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-SCRI.2 — Global Settings › General › Tournament Mode, switched on</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Tournament Mode</b></td><td>One switch turns off every Script, turbo and AI action. Remaps and stick settings stay.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The Script stops, and only runs when you want it.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with the Script's share code.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Power and USB ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-power-and-usb" data-group="Help" data-title="Power and USB problems" data-time="3 min"
  data-keywords="power usb devices cut out disconnect hub charging no light warning aux">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Power and USB problems</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Fix devices that cut out, power warnings and a dark logo.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-power-and-usb--devices-cut-out">
    <h2>My devices cut out</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>Your devices need more power than the console's USB port gives.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Plug the power cable into <b>AUX/POWER</b>.</li>
        <li>Plug its other end into a USB charger or a PC USB port.</li>
        <li>Unplug any device you don't need.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-aux.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the AUX/POWER USB-C port marked, for optional extra power.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-USB.1 — AUX/POWER, the optional power port on the back</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Your devices stay connected through a whole match.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with a list of what's plugged in.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-power-and-usb--power-warning">
    <h2>HOME shows a power warning</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The EXO is running short of power.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Tap the yellow <b>!</b> chip and read the warning.</li>
        <li>Add power on <b>AUX/POWER</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'exo2-ann-health-3.webp' | asset_url }}" width="786" height="603" loading="lazy"
        alt="Part of HOME. A: Your EXO restarted unexpectedly. B: Send report. C: Dismiss. D: a yellow exclamation chip for a warning.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-USB.2 — HOME, with a warning chip (D)</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The <b>!</b> chip goes away.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd><a href="#p-help-get-support">Contact us</a> with a screenshot of the warning.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-power-and-usb--no-light">
    <h2>The EXO doesn't light up</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>No power on the CONSOLE cable, or the config's light is set very dim.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Turn on your console or PC.</li>
        <li>Check the CONSOLE cable is firmly in at both ends.</li>
        <li>Try another USB port on the console or PC.</li>
        <li>In the app, check the config's <b>Brightness</b> on the Device page.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-console.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="436" loading="lazy"
        alt="Close-up of the back of the EXO, with the CONSOLE USB-C port marked. It goes to your console or PC.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-USB.3 — CONSOLE, the USB-C play cable port on the back</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>The logo glows in your config's colour.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Try a USB charger on <b>AUX/POWER</b>, then <a href="#p-help-get-support">contact us</a>.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec m2-symptom" id="p-help-power-and-usb--hub">
    <h2>A USB hub doesn't work</h2>
    <dl class="m2-fix">
      <dt>Likely cause</dt><dd>The hub needs its own power, or it's a type the EXO can't use.</dd>
      <dt>Fix</dt><dd><ol class="m2-steps">
        <li>Use a USB 2.0 hub.</li>
        <li>Give the hub its own power, if it has a power input.</li>
        <li>Add power on <b>AUX/POWER</b>.</li>
      </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-front.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="265" loading="lazy"
        alt="The front of the EXO. One USB-C port on the left and three USB-A ports, for controllers, a mouse and a keyboard.">
      <figcaption>Figure AND-USB.4 — The front of the EXO: one USB-C port and three USB-A ports</figcaption>
    </figure></dd>
      <dt>Fixed when</dt><dd>Devices on the hub show at the top of HOME.</dd>
      <dt>Still stuck?</dt><dd>Plug your devices straight into the EXO's front ports.</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Reset ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-reset" data-group="Help" data-title="Restart, reset and recover" data-time="3 min"
  data-keywords="reset restart reboot factory reset forget re-pair recover start fresh">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Restart, reset and recover</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Start fresh, from a quick restart to pairing your phone again.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">3 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-reset--restart">
    <h2>1. Restart the EXO</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Unplug the CONSOLE cable (and AUX/POWER, if used).</li>
      <li>Wait 5 seconds.</li>
      <li>Plug them back in.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>You can also tap <b>Restart adapter</b> in <b>⋮</b> › <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b>.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig m2-fig--wide">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-hw-back.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="339" loading="lazy"
        alt="The back of the EXO, left to right: CONSOLE, AUX/POWER, AUTH, HDMI IN and HDMI OUT.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-RESE.1 — The back of the EXO, every port named</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <p>Your configs stay saved on the EXO.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-reset--forget-and-repair">
    <h2>2. Forget and pair again</h2>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Close the ZeroStick app.</li>
      <li>Open the app and tap <b>Connect</b>.</li>
      <li>Choose <b>ZeroStick EXO</b>.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-gs-connect.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="712" loading="lazy"
        alt="Connect to your ZeroStick. 1: Connect.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-RESE.2 — Connect to your ZeroStick</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Connect</b></td><td>Then choose ZeroStick EXO in your phone's list.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-reset--config">
    <h2>3. Reset a config</h2>
    <p>The safest way to start a config again is to make a new one: <a href="#p-app-new-config">Make a new config</a>. Then delete the old one:</p>
    <ol class="m2-steps">
      <li>Open the old config's <b>Settings</b> › <b>Device</b> › <b>More</b>.</li>
      <li>Under <b>Danger zone</b>, tap <b>Delete this config</b> (4). It can't be undone.</li>
    </ol>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-sm-light-rows.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="1518" loading="lazy"
        alt="Device, More. 4: Delete this config, in the Danger zone. Nothing in here can be undone.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-RESE.3 — Settings › Device › More, Danger zone</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">4</span></td><td><b>Delete this config</b></td><td>Removes the config. It can't be undone.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-reset--factory">
    <h2>4. Factory reset</h2>
    <p><b>⋮</b> › <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b> has a <b>Danger zone</b> at the bottom with <b>Factory reset — erase phone-app data</b>. It clears the ZeroStick app's data on your phone.</p>
    <figure class="m2-fig">
      <img src="{{ 'man2-dv-support.webp' | asset_url }}" width="700" height="653" loading="lazy"
        alt="Global Settings, General, lower down: Restart adapter, Support with 1: Copy diagnostics, version, config and log, Credits, and Danger zone with Factory reset, erase phone-app data.">
      <figcaption>Figure HELP-RESE.4 — Global Settings › General, lower down</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <table class="m2-legend"><thead><tr><th>No.</th><th>Name</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td><span class="m2-letter m2-letter--num">1</span></td><td><b>Copy diagnostics</b></td><td>Copies your versions, config and log for support.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--warning"><p class="m2-call-label">Warning</p><p>Copy any config you want to keep first, with <b>Copy</b> on the Device page. Then you can paste it back.</p></aside>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-reset--check">
    <h2>Check it worked</h2>
    <aside class="m2-call m2-call--check"><p class="m2-call-label">Check it worked</p>
      <p>You're set when all of these are true:</p>
      <ul><li><b>EXO:</b> the logo lights up again.</li><li><b>App:</b> HOME says <b>Connected</b>.</li><li><b>Console:</b> your controls work.</li></ul>
      <p>Still not right? <a href="#p-help-get-support">Get help from ZeroStick</a></p></aside>
  </section>
</article>

{%- comment -%} ===================== Get support ===================== {%- endcomment -%}
<article class="m2-page" id="p-help-get-support" data-group="Help" data-title="Get help from ZeroStick" data-time="2 min"
  data-keywords="support contact email discord help warranty what to send report">
  <header class="m2-head">
    <p class="m2-crumb">Help</p>
    <h1>Get help from ZeroStick</h1>
    <p class="m2-get">Send us the right details, and we can help on the first reply.</p>
    <div class="m2-badges"><span class="m2-time">2 min</span></div>
  </header>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-get-support--contact">
    <h2>How to reach us</h2>
    <ul class="m2-cards">
      <li><a class="m2-card" href="#support-email"><b>Email</b><span data-m2-email>caleb@zerostickgaming.com</span></a></li>
      <li><a class="m2-card" href="#discord"><b>ZeroStick Discord</b><span>Ask the team and other players.</span></a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="m2-sec" id="p-help-get-support--what-to-send">
    <h2>What to send</h2>
    <div class="m2-table"><table>
      <thead><tr><th>Send</th><th>Where to find it</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>Your platform</b></td><td data-label="Where">PS5 or PC.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>Your game</b></td><td data-label="Where">Under the config name on HOME.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>EXO software version</b></td><td data-label="Where"><b>⋮</b> › <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b>: the pill on the <b>ZeroStick EXO</b> card. Or HOME › tap the EXO card › <b>Board app</b>.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>App version</b></td><td data-label="Where">Tap <b>Copy diagnostics</b> (1) in <b>Global Settings</b> › <b>General</b> › <b>Support</b>. It copies the app and EXO versions, your config and the log. Paste it into your email.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>A screenshot of HOME</b></td><td data-label="Where">Take it on your phone.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>The health report</b></td><td data-label="Where">If HOME says your EXO restarted, tap <b>Send report</b> and paste it in.</td></tr>
        <tr><td data-label="Send"><b>What happened</b></td><td data-label="Where">What you did, what you expected, and what you saw.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table></div>
